WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:06.649
Glass shatters, a D-Class screams, the shrill
cry of the alarm sounds.

00:00:06.649 --> 00:00:10.089
There's been a containment breach at the SCP
Foundation!

00:00:10.089 --> 00:00:15.730
Somehow, The Plague Doctor has escaped his
cell, and is making a break for it!

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:19.200
Against all odds, he finds the exit, and he's
out!

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.790
He's free, he's on the lam!

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:26.010
But how long can he elude the Foundation's
attempts to track him down, and recontain

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:27.440
him at any cost?

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:33.399
It will take all of his cunning, his intellect,
and his strange anomalous abilities, but he's

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:37.559
going to try and hold onto his newfound freedom
as tightly as he can.

00:00:37.559 --> 00:00:39.820
I'm getting ahead of myself here, though.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:41.820
Let's start at the beginning.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.179
Day 1.

00:00:43.179 --> 00:00:49.280
SCP-049, or The Plague Doctor, may be an esoteric
anomaly whose grasp of medicine is practically

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.019
Medieval, but he's still a doctor!

00:00:52.019 --> 00:00:55.280
He didn't get this far by not paying attention
to his surroundings.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:59.819
So, when an unexpected power outage, triggered
by an experiment gone wrong somewhere in the

00:00:59.819 --> 00:01:04.010
bowels of Site-19, gave him the chance to
escape captivity?

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:05.010
He took it.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:10.090
The Foundation had recently revoked his access
to live experimental subjects again, and he

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:11.760
had had enough.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:16.400
It was time to seize the moment and make a
mad dash for freedom.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.290
With the security system down, the Doctor
broke open the door to his cell, grabbed his

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:23.930
trusty apothecary bag, and ran into the hall.

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:29.000
Guards were already swarming, ready to drag
him back into captivity, but he had planned

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.000
ahead.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.400
Swiftly, he uncorked a glass bottle of silvery
liquid, spilling it onto the floor, where

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:39.390
it began to eat away at the tile, the shoes
of the guards, and, if they maintained contact

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:42.740
for too long, the soles of their feet.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:45.290
This bought him just enough time to keep running.

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:50.840
The sounds of screaming down another hall,
and the raucous laughter of one Dr. Jack Bright,

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:55.700
signaled to the Doctor that most of the Foundation
staff were otherwise occupied.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:02:00.920
With this in mind, he sprinted on, letting
his chitinous body carry him to the exit.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:07.560
Then, for the first time in far too long,
fresh air on his beak, the sun in his eyes,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:11.360
the scent of cut grass and damp leaves from
last night's rain.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:16.569
The world was here, waiting for him just as
he had left it.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:19.640
Of course, the world was still very much in
danger.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:24.549
He hadn't just broken free for himself, but
to address the Pestilence head on as best

00:02:24.549 --> 00:02:25.690
he could.

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:29.719
But for now, as he heard the sound of the
alarm, the guards gaining on him, he had to

00:02:29.719 --> 00:02:32.209
prioritize his own safety first.

00:02:32.209 --> 00:02:34.260
He had to hide.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.260
Day 2.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:40.129
He ran for ages, he couldn't be quite sure
how long as he had no way to measure the passage

00:02:40.129 --> 00:02:43.650
of time except the position of the sun in
the sky.

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:49.680
It set, it rose, bathing the countryside in
soft yellow light, and set again, plunging

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:54.170
the land into darkness, all while he continued
to run.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:57.209
Then, finally, the Plague Doctor stopped.

00:02:57.209 --> 00:02:58.499
He had found a farm.

00:02:58.499 --> 00:03:03.560
There was a little farmhouse, but he did not
dare disturb the sleeping family and alarm

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:04.560
them.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.260
Instead, he turned to the barn for shelter.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:11.300
He let himself in, tiptoed past the horses
as they slept there, and made himself a bed

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.510
from straw and a burlap sack.

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:16.739
From his bag, he pulled a pillow, and a little
spray bottle.

00:03:16.739 --> 00:03:22.260
He misted the pillow with a lavender scented
oil, and finally allowed himself a moment

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:23.260
to rest.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:28.419
He did not need to sleep like ordinary men,
but after such a long journey, he could get

00:03:28.419 --> 00:03:29.419
pretty close.

00:03:29.419 --> 00:03:30.739
Day 3.

00:03:30.739 --> 00:03:34.310
The morning of the Plague Doctor's third day
of freedom began with the high-pitched whinny

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:38.099
of a terrified horse, and the frantic stamping
of hooves.

00:03:38.099 --> 00:03:42.430
The Doctor opened his eyes to the sight of
one of the horses, now awake and not at all

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:47.049
happy to see a stranger in its barn, making
its fear and displeasure known.

00:03:47.049 --> 00:03:48.049
"Buttercup?"

00:03:48.049 --> 00:03:49.739
A man called from outside the barn.

00:03:49.739 --> 00:03:51.049
"That you, girl?

00:03:51.049 --> 00:03:52.169
What's got you spooked?"

00:03:52.169 --> 00:03:56.519
The door to the barn creaked open, and before
the Doctor could do anything, he was face

00:03:56.519 --> 00:03:58.840
to face with the farmer who owned the land.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.720
"Who are you and what are you doing in my
barn?"

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:02.760
The man demanded.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.269
"Good sir, I apologize for the intrusion!

00:04:05.269 --> 00:04:07.849
I am but a humble traveler, seeking shelter-"

00:04:07.849 --> 00:04:10.749
"You need to get out of here and stop scaring
my horses, now!

00:04:10.749 --> 00:04:13.140
Don't make me come back with my shotgun."

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.780
"No need for that sort of thing!

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:17.370
I will be on my way!"

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:21.280
The Doctor collected his things, and, deciding
to spare the old farmer rather than using

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:26.389
more extreme methods to change his mind, left
the barn in a hurry.

00:04:26.389 --> 00:04:28.340
Day 4.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:32.610
With the farm far behind him, the Plague Doctor
trudged along on his journey, always keeping

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:35.830
an eye out for unmarked vans and armed guards.

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:38.000
So far, though, he was safe.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.600
He hadn't had a spare moment to return to
his experiments, though, which was beginning

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:43.849
to wear on him.

00:04:43.849 --> 00:04:47.960
The work was what had motivated him to break
out in the first place, and now he wasn't

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:50.590
sure when he would be able to make time for
it.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.259
Cruel irony indeed.

00:04:52.259 --> 00:04:57.830
But then, as if his silent prayer had been
answered, he heard a peculiar sound coming

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:01.879
from the woods just off the dirt road he was
walking down.

00:05:01.879 --> 00:05:04.110
A sickly bray, from an injured animal.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:05.979
A poor soul in need.

00:05:05.979 --> 00:05:06.979
A patient!

00:05:06.979 --> 00:05:12.210
He followed the sound to its source: a deer
lay on its side, clearly sick or injured somehow.

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:14.639
"Do not be afraid, my friend."

00:05:14.639 --> 00:05:15.979
The Doctor said softly.

00:05:15.979 --> 00:05:18.440
"You are sick, but I can make you well."

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:21.240
He sat his bag down on the grass, and got
to work.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:25.849
First, he touched the deer with a gloved hand,
stopping its heart and putting it out of its

00:05:25.849 --> 00:05:26.849
misery.

00:05:26.849 --> 00:05:31.430
Then, he reached into his bag for his trusty
tools and some of his best medicines.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:37.020
In no time at all, the deer was reanimated,
cured, walking around again like new.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:42.039
Sure, it was a little bit different, stumbling
a bit, and each eye looked in a different

00:05:42.039 --> 00:05:45.490
direction, but the Doctor considered the treatment
a success.

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:47.979
A day well-spent!

00:05:47.979 --> 00:05:48.979
Day 5

00:05:48.979 --> 00:05:53.150
The next day, feeling reinvigorated after
his successful encounter with the deer, the

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:56.100
Plague Doctor began his quest for shelter
anew.

00:05:56.100 --> 00:06:01.669
He walked most of the day, until, as the sun
was setting, he came upon something curious:

00:06:01.669 --> 00:06:08.240
a house, dilapidated-looking, with a large
sign out front: "House of Horrors, Enter if

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:09.430
You Dare."

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:14.560
Though he didn't know it, the Doctor had stumbled
upon the local town's premiere seasonal haunted

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:15.930
house attraction.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:20.080
To him, it was simply an empty house he could
take up residence inside.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:25.610
He was curious, and a bit perplexed, as he
walked past plastic skeletons, animatronic

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:31.129
werewolves that popped out from behind styrofoam
tombstones, and giant fake spiders in cotton

00:06:31.129 --> 00:06:32.379
cobwebs.

00:06:32.379 --> 00:06:37.139
None of the fake monsters gave him trouble,
so, though he was confused by what he saw,

00:06:37.139 --> 00:06:39.360
he continued to explore the house.

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:44.099
Then, he found something incredible: a laboratory.

00:06:44.099 --> 00:06:47.580
There was a long stainless steel table, with
a mannequin strapped to it.

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:52.750
A row of prop surgical tools sat on a tray
next to the mannequin, and along a back shelf

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:56.949
were rows and rows of jars filled with liquids
that looked like something the Plague Doctor

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:59.139
himself would pull out of his bag.

00:06:59.139 --> 00:07:05.450
He couldn't believe his eyes, after wandering
aimlessly for days he had found the perfect

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:06.450
place.

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:09.810
Almost as if it had been made just for him.

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:14.010
Of course, it wasn't, it was for the paying
customers who would be coming to the haunted

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:19.470
house the next day, along with the actors
hired to perform inside, but he didn't need

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:21.319
to know any of that yet.

00:07:21.319 --> 00:07:24.930
He replaced the jars with his own, and the
tools with functioning ones.

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:29.080
With the exception of the plastic body on
the table, which he privately wished was a

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:33.000
real human subject, this was absolutely perfect.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:38.229
Day 6, the haunt actors showed up for work,
and were surprised to find a new guy had beat

00:07:38.229 --> 00:07:40.960
them there, and he was already in costume.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:46.340
They shrugged it off, they were making minimum
wage and that wasn't enough to ask any questions.

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:49.939
They were there to suit up and get spooky,
and that was it.

00:07:49.939 --> 00:07:52.190
They did appreciate his plague doctor costume,
though.

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:54.849
It was much higher-budget than anything they
had.

00:07:54.849 --> 00:07:56.750
"Did you make that getup yourself?"

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:58.389
Asked a friendly zombie.

00:07:58.389 --> 00:07:59.620
"Indeed, I did!"

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:03.379
The Doctor replied cheerfully, happy to finally
encounter a group of individuals who were

00:08:03.379 --> 00:08:04.379
unafraid of him.

00:08:04.379 --> 00:08:05.430
"Nice, bro!"

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:09.889
The zombie gave him a thumbs-up, and if the
Plague Doctor could have with his rigid beaked

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:12.009
face, he would have smiled.

00:08:12.009 --> 00:08:17.520
These new colleagues were a bit unusual-looking,
with their ghostly white faces, vampire fangs,

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:22.410
green-tinged makeup and excess fur, but their
kindness was encouraging.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:26.810
Meanwhile, the haunt actors were gossiping
amongst themselves, wondering where the new

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:29.160
plague doctor character came from.

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:30.240
Who approved it?

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:31.749
Who hired this guy?

00:08:31.749 --> 00:08:33.340
Why was he doing that accent?

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:40.839
Whatever, he was plenty scary and a nice enough
guy to work with, so Frankenstein's Monster

00:08:40.839 --> 00:08:45.550
let the Plague Doctor have the laboratory
set, and moved himself into the graveyard.

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:50.410
The customers loved him too, shrieking with
delight as he welcomed them into his laboratory,

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:53.660
asking if any of them would like to volunteer
to be a test subject.

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:57.709
Lucky for them, they had already been warned
not to touch any of the "actors" while walking

00:08:57.709 --> 00:08:59.220
through the attraction.

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:04.080
As his first night at his unintentional job
came to a close, the Plague Doctor's new friends

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:05.080
bid him farewell.

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:08.260
"We're going to a bar up the road for a couple
drinks!"

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:09.589
The ghostly bridge said.

00:09:09.589 --> 00:09:10.589
"Wanna come?"

00:09:10.589 --> 00:09:12.630
"Ah, no time for revelry!"

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:13.630
The Plague Doctor replied.

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:15.730
"I must attend to my work.

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:16.730
Take care!"

00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:17.730
The woman just laughed.

00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:19.089
"Okay, see you later."

00:09:19.089 --> 00:09:23.100
And so the Plague Doctor spent his night in
the haunted house again, tinkering with his

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:28.700
tools and his tissue samples, listening to
the royalty-free scary music tape play again

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:31.670
and again on repeat, into the night.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:32.670
Day 7.

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:35.920
The next day, attendance at the haunted house
was slow.

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:40.040
The actors, with little to do, spent their
time scrolling aimlessly on their phones,

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:43.769
filming joke videos for social media, and
pranking each other.

00:09:43.769 --> 00:09:47.510
One of them got the bright idea to pull a
prank on the new hire, the stranger that none

00:09:47.510 --> 00:09:49.240
of them knew much about.

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:52.950
He would have a friend, turn out the lights
in the laboratory, and when the lights were

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:56.610
turned back on, he would have replaced the
mannequin on the table.

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:58.850
He couldn't have known what would happen.

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:03.470
All he wanted to do was startle the new guy,
freak him out with the sight of an unexpected

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:05.339
werewolf on his operating table.

00:10:05.339 --> 00:10:08.949
And it was effective- sort of.

00:10:08.949 --> 00:10:12.699
The Plague Doctor froze in place when the
lights went out, calling, "Hello?

00:10:12.699 --> 00:10:13.699
What is happening?"

00:10:13.699 --> 00:10:17.680
and when the room was illuminated once more,
he took in the sight of the living being on

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:18.680
the operating table.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:19.680
"My friend!

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.580
You have come to me for treatment?"

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:25.089
The werewolf started to get up, disappointed
he hadn't managed to elicit a scream, but

00:10:25.089 --> 00:10:29.430
the Plague Doctor reached out a hand to stop
him, and that was curtains for that particular

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:30.430
actor.

00:10:30.430 --> 00:10:34.029
As soon as the Plague Doctor's gloved hand
made contact with the man in the werewolf

00:10:34.029 --> 00:10:36.250
costume, his heart stopped.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:37.480
"Oh dear."

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:38.600
The Plague Doctor remarked.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:40.460
"Do not fear, I have the cure.

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:43.830
You'll be alright in no time at all"
By the time the rest of the actors came to

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:48.220
see what had happened to the werewolf, there
was a real zombie in the haunted house.

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:51.290
Then, it was pure chaos.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:55.670
Actors running and screaming, knocking over
props and abandoning their seasonal gig, darting

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:59.470
between customers as they went, shrieking
"Don't go in there!

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:00.470
It's real!"

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:03.350
Naturally, this only made them want to check
it out even more.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:07.600
But by the time they got inside, there was
no sign of the Plague Doctor.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:14.250
Only one very lost zombie in a werewolf costume,
a few jars broken in all the chaos, and footsteps

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:17.980
in the dry grass outside, leading out of town.

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:19.589
Days 8 to 18

00:11:19.589 --> 00:11:23.959
The Plague Doctor spent all of his eighth
day on the run walking, once more.

00:11:23.959 --> 00:11:27.990
He was starting to get used to this, the endless
drudgery of the path to freedom.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:32.940
He hated to admit it, but he was almost starting
to miss his cell back at the Foundation, the

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:37.910
routine of it, the quiet time to work, the
three meals given to him each day even though

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:40.300
he didn't need to eat to survive.

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:45.000
He missed food and drink, the simple pleasures
of bread, meat, cheese, fruit.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.730
A mug of tea, a cup of wine.

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:49.649
He sighed to himself, wistfully.

00:11:49.649 --> 00:11:52.519
Then, he caught a whiff of something lovely.

00:11:52.519 --> 00:11:55.810
He lifted his beak, taking another deep breath.

00:11:55.810 --> 00:12:00.209
The unmistakable scent of roast pheasant,
hearty and warm.

00:12:00.209 --> 00:12:02.290
Beneath it, something else.

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:05.089
Mulled wine, spiced and inviting.

00:12:05.089 --> 00:12:08.970
Smells that reminded him of home, of days
long lost.

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:12.980
He couldn't be certain where it would lead,
or if there would be a seat for him at the

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:17.730
table, but he couldn't resist following the
heavenly aroma to its source.

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:21.850
As he drew closer to the smell of food and
merriment, he could hear music.

00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:26.690
The plucking of a lyre, the high trill of
a flute, singing and clapping.

00:12:26.690 --> 00:12:29.019
Then, he finally spotted it.

00:12:29.019 --> 00:12:34.009
Rows of colorful tents, long banquet tables,
minstrels wandering about and playing ballads

00:12:34.009 --> 00:12:35.810
to anyone who would listen.

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:42.490
Men, women, and children frolicking in elaborate
costumes, plate armor, robes, gowns, and more.

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:46.389
Though the Plague Doctor didn't know how to
describe what he was seeing, he had wandered

00:12:46.389 --> 00:12:50.339
onto the site of one of the state's largest
Renaissance Faires.

00:12:50.339 --> 00:12:55.540
It just so happened to be opening day, and
he was just in time for the celebratory feast.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:56.839
"Good day, Doctor!"

00:12:56.839 --> 00:12:59.259
A nobleman tipped his hat to SCP-049.

00:12:59.259 --> 00:13:02.139
"Are you speaking to me?"

00:13:02.139 --> 00:13:04.160
The Plague Doctor was taken aback by the recognition.

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:07.770
"Why of course, you're the only doctor I see!

00:13:07.770 --> 00:13:11.980
Her Majesty the Queen thanks you for your
service, for keeping us all safe from the

00:13:11.980 --> 00:13:13.199
great plague!"

00:13:13.199 --> 00:13:17.470
The Plague Doctor had no idea that this man
was an actor, playing along with him in what

00:13:17.470 --> 00:13:19.870
he assumed was a scene for the tourists.

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:24.630
Instead, he took the words to heart, swelling
with pride and gratitude for the recognition.

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:29.020
"Good sir, it is my duty and my honor."

00:13:29.020 --> 00:13:31.150
The Plague Doctor nodded politely.

00:13:31.150 --> 00:13:35.351
Luckily for him, and unbeknownst to the rest
of the cast of players at the Faire, the man

00:13:35.351 --> 00:13:39.520
originally hired to play the town Plague Doctor
had booked a commercial role that morning

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:41.710
and had decided not to go in to work.

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:47.400
That man's choice not to call and let anyone
know, though rude, led to a fortuitous misunderstanding

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:49.079
for SCP-049.

00:13:49.079 --> 00:13:52.220
"Please, join us at the Royal Table!"

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:56.290
The nobleman made a sweeping gesture with
his arm, inviting the doctor to sit and dine

00:13:56.290 --> 00:13:59.490
with him and the rest of the actors playing
members of the court.

00:13:59.490 --> 00:14:01.600
"Thank you for your kindness."

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:03.870
If he could, the Plague Doctor would have
smiled.

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:09.220
He dined to his heart's content that afternoon,
listening to sounds of music and laughter.

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:14.180
He slotted into his role at the Faire even
better than his position at the Haunted House.

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:18.371
He answered questions from tourists about
his work as a physician, warned them of the

00:14:18.371 --> 00:14:23.070
dangers of the Great Pestilence, and posed
for the occasional photograph.

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:28.040
He spent a wonderful ten days living in a
stylized, artificial version of the past,

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:32.760
basking in the warm glow of camaraderie - though
the other actors wondered why he never took

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:34.810
his mask off, even to eat.

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:38.250
Then, sadly, it was time for the Faire to
pack up for the season.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:42.709
The Plague Doctor bid his new friends farewell,
and declined their offers to exchange numbers

00:14:42.709 --> 00:14:44.009
and keep in touch.

00:14:44.009 --> 00:14:47.389
He would, however, always remember them fondly.

00:14:47.389 --> 00:14:49.290
Days 19-41

00:14:49.290 --> 00:14:53.280
As he was departing the Faire grounds, the
Doctor caught a glimpse of strange men approaching

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:57.490
some of the actors, showing federal badges
and asking them questions.

00:14:57.490 --> 00:15:02.370
He couldn't be certain that it was the Foundation,
but it was more than enough to make him cautious.

00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:06.610
He would have to retreat into the woods once
more, and stay out of sight.

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:12.819
He laid low for quite some time, for 22 days
to be exact, but then, on Day 41…

00:15:12.819 --> 00:15:14.930
Day 41 to 52.

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:16.660
It started to snow.

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:19.560
White blanketed the forest floor, soft and
cold.

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:23.350
The weather wouldn't kill him, of course,
but it was uncomfortable.

00:15:23.350 --> 00:15:27.329
He would need to find some more efficient
shelter, to escape from the elements before

00:15:27.329 --> 00:15:29.220
the winter storm worsened.

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:33.259
He trudged through the snow, into a new town,
small and quaint.

00:15:33.259 --> 00:15:37.410
There was an abandoned church at the edge
of the main road, a bit broken down, but the

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:42.240
roof held firm against the onslaught of ice
and wind, so the Plague Doctor made it his

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:47.480
new home for the next 12 days, working quietly
and staying out of sight.

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:49.500
Day 53 to 57.

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:54.310
On the eve of the Plague Doctor's 53rd day
on the run from the SCP Foundation, he was

00:15:54.310 --> 00:15:58.200
stirred from his work by the sound of a choir
of beautiful voices outside.

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:03.490
He looked, to find a group of Christmas Carolers
singing together, the rows of houses along

00:16:03.490 --> 00:16:07.810
the streets covered in colorful lights and
glittering decorations.

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:11.940
Wanting to get a little closer to the music,
the Doctor left his hiding spot for the first

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:14.310
time in nearly two weeks.

00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:18.910
But as the choir saw a strangely shaped dark
shadow, emerging from the abandoned church,

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:21.949
they screamed and scattered in every direction.

00:16:21.949 --> 00:16:25.699
One of them yelled something about "the Krampus"
as they went.

00:16:25.699 --> 00:16:31.480
Frightened by the whole interaction, SCP-049
found himself a new spot, under a bridge.

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:33.279
It was cold, but isolated.

00:16:33.279 --> 00:16:36.860
At least, it was for five days.

00:16:36.860 --> 00:16:37.860
Day 58.

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:43.160
On day 58, a group of local teenagers, rowdy
and looking to make some trouble, spotted

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:45.310
the Plague Doctor squatting under the bridge.

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:47.990
They pelted him with snowballs, laughing.

00:16:47.990 --> 00:16:52.579
Before he could do anything about it, fortunately
for the teens, they ran back to their car

00:16:52.579 --> 00:16:53.740
and sped away.

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:58.629
Drenched in ice and cold water, miserable,
and irritated, the Plague Doctor searched

00:16:58.629 --> 00:17:00.430
for another place to stay.

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:03.000
Day 59 to Day 84

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:08.030
The Plague Doctor was able to slip into another
relatively quiet building: the local community

00:17:08.030 --> 00:17:12.770
theatre, which happened to be an old opera
house repurposed as the site of volunteer-run

00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:13.770
musicals.

00:17:13.770 --> 00:17:18.140
While the townsfolk began rehearsals for their
production of The Phantom of the Opera, the

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:21.740
Plague Doctor watched from above, hiding in
the shadows.

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:26.400
Every so often, the stagehand would catch
a glimpse of a cape, the silhouette of a face,

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:30.890
a pair of dark eyes, but no one believed her
when she tried to tell them that the Phantom

00:17:30.890 --> 00:17:31.980
was real.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:37.090
At least, until a handyman went up into the
rafters to install some lights, and saw the

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:38.409
Plague Doctor for himself.

00:17:38.409 --> 00:17:42.150
Then, it was time for him to flee to a new
town.

00:17:42.150 --> 00:17:44.410
DAY 85 TO DAY 89

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:49.270
On Day 85, the Plague Doctor climbed up onto
the roof of a dark house to avoid a particularly

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:53.080
aggressive dog, and let himself in through
the attic window.

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:57.740
The next morning, a little girl came up into
the attic in search of a lost toy, and found

00:17:57.740 --> 00:17:58.740
him there.

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:01.760
He waited for her to scream, but she didn't.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:06.080
She introduced herself as Abby, and asked
if he would like some cookies and milk.

00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:10.750
He accepted her gracious offer, and the two
visited with each other for several days,

00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:13.380
until Abby's parents asked who she was talking
to.

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:17.940
They didn't take it well when she answered,
"The bird man in the attic."

00:18:17.940 --> 00:18:18.940
DAY 90

00:18:18.940 --> 00:18:22.931
On Day 90, Abby's parents called the police,
who, having been warned to look out for a

00:18:22.931 --> 00:18:28.190
man in a "bird mask," got in touch with their
contacts at the SCP Foundation.

00:18:28.190 --> 00:18:33.020
Feeling the authorities closing in, SCP-049
took to the wilderness once more.

00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:35.750
DAY 91 T0 DAY 99

00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:39.980
Though the air was still painfully cold, The
Plague Doctor managed to set up camp, using

00:18:39.980 --> 00:18:43.640
tools from his bag to build a fire and construct
a makeshift tent.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:48.159
He stayed there for three days before intending
to move on and throw the Foundation off of

00:18:48.159 --> 00:18:52.630
his trail, but he was slowed by the appearance
of a group of hikers, bundled up against the

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:55.070
Winter weather and exploring the woods.

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:59.270
Afraid he couldn't trust them, the Doctor
touched one, to convince him to leave.

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:03.871
The man fell to the ground, dead, and as his
companions ran away screaming, the Doctor

00:19:03.871 --> 00:19:05.580
vowed to cure him.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:10.270
Working against the inopportune conditions,
it took him five more days to reanimate the

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:11.270
hiker.

00:19:11.270 --> 00:19:12.270
DAY 100

00:19:12.270 --> 00:19:15.820
On Day 100 of his time on the lam, the Foundation
finally closed in.

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:19.790
The Plague Doctor was just stitching up a
large incision in his patient's chest, when

00:19:19.790 --> 00:19:21.880
he heard the click of a gun behind him.

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:26.010
"Come with us peacefully, and we won't have
to sedate you," the officer said.

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:30.750
With a heavy sigh, the Plague Doctor held
up his hands, stepping back from his patient

00:19:30.750 --> 00:19:35.440
just as its undead body sat up, blinking its
unseeing eyes.

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:36.490
"Very well.

00:19:36.490 --> 00:19:38.600
I will go back.

00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:42.730
To tell you the truth, gentlemen, this has
all been a bit too much trouble.

00:19:42.730 --> 00:19:44.730
I could use the rest."

00:19:44.730 --> 00:19:52.570
Now go check out "SCP-049 - the Plague Doctor
Captured" and "SCP-049 Cures SCP-096 of the

00:19:52.570 --> 00:19:53.570
Pestilence?!"

00:19:53.570 --> 00:19:54.760
for more of your favorite mysterious masked
Doctor!

